        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "KM PROPERTY are delighted to bring to market Robbswall Cottage, a truly exceptional and private residence, set on 1.58 acre of seafront land with magnificent views over Low Rock in Malahide and beyond. Extending to more than 372 sq.m. / 4,000 sq.ft., this exclusive home presents a rare opportunity that has not been seen on the North Dublin market in recent memory.\n\n\nViewing video https://youtu.be/W1-dBDTZ2oo\n\nSurrounded by manicured and beautifully landscaped grounds, the property comprises the main residence together with a coach house, boat house, stables and a private tennis court a setting that combines coastal tranquillity with genuine country-estate scale, just minutes from Malahide village.\n\n\nUniquely, Robbswall Cottage is arranged in three distinct sections, each with its own character and charm, yet connected to allow the entire property to be opened up into one magnificent and cohesive home. This flexibility offers extraordinary scope whether for multi-generational living, guest and staff accommodation, or simply a home of immense scale and versatility.\n\n\nIn total, the house offers six to eight bedrooms and five bathrooms across its three interconnecting sections an outstanding and rare proposition in this most sought-after of seafront settings.\n\n\nAT A GLANCE\n\n\nLocation: Robbswall, Malahide, Co. Dublin overlooking Low Rock\nSize: 372 sq.m. / 4,000+ sq.ft. of accommodation\n\n\nGrounds: Just over one acre of seafront, manicured and landscaped grounds\n\n\nBedrooms: 6 8, across three interconnecting sections\n\n\nBathrooms: 5\n\n\nOutbuildings: Coach house, boat house, stables and tennis court\n\n\nConfiguration: Three distinct sections can be combined into one magnificent home\n\n\nAsking Price: 2,900,000\n\n\nSECTION ONE THE PRINCIPAL HOUSE\n\nApproached through a welcoming hallway, this is the principal part of the home and showcases beautifully proportioned, light-filled reception rooms.\n\n\nEntrance hallway\nLiving room\n\nKitchen / dining room\n\nOffice / second reception room\n\nConservatory\n\nUpstairs:\n\n\nThree double bedrooms\n\nMaster bedroom with en suite\n\nMain bathroom\n\nA further double room off bedroom three currently used as a home gym, with potential to be reconfigured as bedroom seven\n\nSECTION TWO THE GARDEN WING\n\nConnected from the principal house, yet capable of being divided to stand independently, this wing offers wonderfully flexible living and entertaining space.\n\n\nUtility room\n\nKitchen\n\nMusic room / living room\n\nWC\n\nStorage\n\nUpstairs:\n\n\nTwo bedrooms\n\nMain bathroom\n\nSECTION THREE THE COTTAGE\n\nAccessed independently via its own car port, this charming and versatile wing can equally be opened up to the main house. It enjoys its own private garden with sea views and its own separate driveway around the perimeter of the property ideal as guest or staff accommodation, or as an income-generating annexe.\n\n\nKitchen / living room\n\nDining room\n\nUtility room\n\nUpstairs:\n\n\nA sixth bedroom\n\nA further large living room, with potential to be reconfigured as bedroom eight\n\n\nPrivate garden with sea views and its own separate driveway around the perimeter of the property.\n\n\nTHE GROUNDS & OUTBUILDINGS\n\nSet on just over an acre of seafront land, the gardens at Robbswall Cottage have been manicured and landscaped to the highest standard, framing the house and its outbuildings with mature planting and sweeping lawns with views over Low Rock.\n\n\nCoach house\n\nBoat house\n\nStables\n\nPrivate tennis court\n\nSea views over Low Rock, Malahide\n\nSeparate perimeter driveway serving the Cottage\n\n\nTogether, these grounds and outbuildings create a genuinely rare estate setting, with scope for equestrian use, boating, tennis and entertaining all within a private seafront position close to Malahide village.\n\n\nA TRULY SPECIAL HOME\n\nWith its rare combination of scale, privacy and flexibility, Robbswall Cottage stands apart. The ability to configure the property as three distinct sections or to open them up into one magnificent residence of up to eight bedrooms gives this home an adaptability seldom found at this level of the market.\n\n\nCombined with its seafront setting overlooking Low Rock, its manicured grounds extending to just over an acre, and its outstanding outbuildings including a coach house, boat house, stables and private tennis court, this is a residence like nothing else to have come to the North Dublin market.\n\n\nOutstanding. \nExclusive. \nUnrepeatable.\n\n\nFOR PRIVATE VIEWING AND FURTHER INFORMATION\n| E: info@kmproperty.ie | www.kmproperty.ie\n\n\nKaren O`Driscoll, Managing Director\n.\n\nThese particulars are issued by KM PROPERTY on the understanding that any negotiations relating to the property are conducted through them. While every care has been taken in preparing these particulars, they do not constitute any part of an offer or contract. All descriptions, dimensions, references to condition and necessary permissions for use and occupation are given in good faith and are believed to be correct, but any intending purchaser should not rely on them as statements of fact and should satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to their accuracy. Floor areas, room sizes and bedroom/bathroom configurations are approximate and subject to verification."
